Given the functions $f(x)=\ln x$ and $g(x)=\frac{m(x+n)}{x+1} (m > 0)$.

$(1)$ If the function $y=f(x)$ and $y=g(x)$ have the same tangent line at $x=1$, find the value of $m$;

$(2)$ If for all $x \geqslant 1$, the inequality $|f(x)| \geqslant |g(x)|$ always holds, find the maximum value of the real number $m$.

In $\triangle ABC$, the sides opposite to angles $A$, $B$, $C$ are $a$, $b$, $c$ respectively, and $\sqrt{3}b\cos A=a\sin B$.

$(1)$ Find the size of angle $A$;

$(2)$ If $a=6$ and the area of $\triangle ABC$ is $9\sqrt{3}$, find the lengths of sides $b$ and $c$.

(1) The sum of the first $n$ terms of an arithmetic sequence $\{a\_n\}$ is $S\_n$. Given that $a\_{m-1}+a\_{m+1}-a\_m^{2}=0$, $S\_{2m-1}=38$, find $m$;
(2) The sum of the first $n$ terms of an arithmetic sequence $\{a\_n\}$ is $S\_n$. If $S\_3=9$, $S\_6=36$, find $a\_7+a\_8+a\_9$;
(3) The sum of the first three terms of an arithmetic sequence is 34, the sum of the last three terms is 146, and the sum of all terms is 390. Find the number of terms in this sequence;
(4) The general term formula of the sequence $\{a\_n\}$ is $a\_n=4n-25$. Find the sum of the first $n$ terms of the sequence $\{|a\_n|\}$ and state the basic method to determine whether a sequence is an arithmetic sequence.

