A study group consists of students and teachers, and the composition of the group meets the following three conditions:

(1) The number of male students is greater than the number of female students;  
(2) The number of female students is greater than the number of teachers;  
(3) The number of teachers doubled is more than the number of male students.  
① If the number of teachers is $4$, then the maximum number of female students is $\boxed{6}$.  

② The minimum number of people in the group is $\boxed{12}$.

Given an ellipse $C:\frac{{x}^{2}}{{a}^{2}}+\frac{{y}^{2}}{{b}^{2}}=1(a>b>0)$ with eccentricity $\frac{\sqrt{2}}{2}$, point $A\left(2,1\right)$ lies on the ellipse $C$.  
