Given the parametric equations of curve $C_1$: $$\begin{cases} x=\cos\theta \\ y=1+\sin\theta \end{cases}$$ (where $\theta$ is the parameter), and establishing a polar coordinate system with the origin as the pole and the positive half-axis of the x-axis as the polar axis, the polar equation of curve $C_2$ is: $\rho=4\sin\left(\theta+ \frac{\pi}{3}\right)$, and the polar equation of line $l$ is $\theta= \frac{\pi}{6}$.  
