$\frac{2}{{\sqrt{5}+\sqrt{3}}}=\frac{{2(\sqrt{5}-\sqrt{3})}}{{(\sqrt{5}+\sqrt{3})(\sqrt{5}-\sqrt{3})}}=\frac{{2(\sqrt{5}-\sqrt{3})}}{{{{(\sqrt{5})}^2}-{{(\sqrt{3})}^2}}}=\frac{{2(\sqrt{5}-\sqrt{3})}}{{5-3}}=\sqrt{5}-\sqrt{3}$;  
