The cells of a $40 \times 40$ table are colored in $n$ colors such that for any cell, all $n$ colors can be found within the union of its row and column. Find the maximum possible number of blue cells if:

(a) $n=2$;

(b) $n=20$.

The sum of the first $n$ terms of the sequence $\{a_n\}$ is denoted as $S_n$, with $a_1=t$. The point $(S_n, a_{n+1})$ lies on the line $y=2x+1$, where $n\in\mathbb{N}^*$.  
(1) If the sequence $\{a_n\}$ is a geometric sequence, find the value of the real number $t$;  
