(where \(\alpha\) is the parameter).
- (1) Find the length of the chord that the circle cuts off from the line;
- (2) If a line \(m\) passing through \(P(0,-2)\) intersects the circle at two distinct points \(A\) and \(B\), find \(\overrightarrow{PA} \cdot \overrightarrow{PB}\).

Given an ellipse $C$ with foci $F_{1}(-2\sqrt{2}, 0)$, $F_{2}(2\sqrt{2}, 0)$, and a moving point $P$ on it satisfies $|PF_{1}|+|PF_{2}|=4\sqrt{3}$. Let point $O$ be the origin, and the lower vertex of ellipse $C$ be $R$.
(Ⅰ) Find the standard equation of ellipse $C$;
(Ⅱ) Suppose a line $l_{2}$ passing through the point $(0, 1)$ with slope $k$ intersects ellipse $C$ at points $M$ and $N$, investigate whether $\overrightarrow{RM} \cdot \overrightarrow{RN}$ is always a constant value regardless of the value of $k$. If yes, find the constant value; if not, explain why.

A factory produces a type of instrument. Due to limitations in production capacity and technical level, some defective products are produced. According to experience, the defect rate $p$ of the factory producing this instrument is generally related to the daily output $x$ (pieces) as follows: 
$$
P= \begin{cases} 
\frac {1}{96-x} & (1\leq x\leq 94, x\in \mathbb{N}) \\ 
\frac {2}{3} & (x>94, x\in \mathbb{N})
\end{cases}
$$
It is known that for every qualified instrument produced, a profit of $A$ yuan can be made, but for every defective product produced, a loss of $\frac {A}{2}$ yuan will be incurred. The factory wishes to determine an appropriate daily output.
(1) Determine whether producing this instrument can be profitable when the daily output (pieces) exceeds 94 pieces, and explain the reason;
